  "hypothesis": "H79-DCMS (Dip-Coupled Multi-Scale Scarp, Bedrock Reactivation & Hydrothermal Conduit Network): Unmapped Quaternary geothermal conduit, splay, and basin-bounding faults across the Great Basin produce a coupled structural signature combining (i) multi-scale 10-m USGS 3DEP DEM scarp steps (100 m, 300 m, 700 m, 1,500 m) closing the 25.5% Nevada 1-m LiDAR gap plus strike-steered scarp anisotropy, (ii) USGS DS-1052 State Geologic Map Compilation pre-Quaternary bedrock fault reactivation corridors, (iii) DOE GDR 1391 2-m shallow temperature residuals, Quaternary sinter/travertine/tufa upflow vents, spring clusters, and volcanic vent conduits, and (iv) fold-fair multi-scale crack-tip and colinear relay fields coupled multiplicatively with scarp prominence, SGMC bedrock structure, geodetic dilatation/shear rate, and hydrothermal alteration.",
  "mechanism": "Two-stage nested spatially-blocked 4-quadrant OOF ensemble (Stage-1 LightGBM + Stage-2 LightGBM + standard-scaled MLP with pooled OOF isotonic probability calibration) estimates exact-pixel posterior p(x) and 300-m triangular-kernel credit q_300m(x) over 118 physical and fold-fair visible-catalogue channels (zero fold leakage). A median-scale Dinkelbach submodular 300-m kernel allocator selects non-overlapping fault pixels on inner simulated worlds (lambda_fp=0.235, min_sep_px=1.85, max_budget=37500), emitting 36,404 natural-equilibrium pixels across all 4 quadrants.",
  "named_non_fault_mimic": "Pleistocene pluvial paleo-shoreline wave-cut benches (Lake Lahontan and Lake Bonneville), fluvial terrace risers along the Humboldt/Carson/Walker rivers, welded ash-flow caldera cooling joints, erosional range-front pediment breaks above non-faulted bedrock contacts, and down-gradient lateral thermal outflow plumes in permeable alluvial fans.",
